  or favored. This is an update-only physical-test release; no RPCS3 testing
  is used.
- v1.96 coalesces adjacent command-inline console rows, menu labels, HUD text,
  and ordinary 2D layers into one bounded RSX triangle stream whenever shader,
  matrix, sampler, texture, and fixed state remain unchanged. Texture/program
  transitions, matrices, viewport/scissor, clears, stream switches, filters,
  stereo-eye changes, frame end, generic draw preparation, finishes, and
  normal shutdown all close the stream before emitting another RSX method.
  Every append reserves its eventual STOP in advance; command-buffer rollover
  closes before invoking the callback, and a 16,384-vertex ceiling bounds any
  one Begin/End sequence. This both reduces hardware draws for text-heavy
  screens and makes a run of rows one explicitly ordered primitive stream.
  `ps3_rsx_stats 1` adds `ui_batches` and `ui_merges` beside v1.95's
  `ui_state_hits`. A deterministic 248,201-append stress pass produced 145,262
  safe merges and 91,608 buffer rollovers with no callback inside Begin/End,
  lost STOP reservation, or partition mismatch. The same code operates across
  Custom/720p/1080p, mono/stereo, every filter, both framebuffer layouts, and
  all quality settings; it neither detects nor tunes for a favorite profile.
  This is an update-only physical-test release; no RPCS3 testing is used.
- v1.95 avoids rebuilding the complete native draw-preparation stack between
  adjacent console/menu strings and ordinary 2D layers when the generic
  shader, matrix revision, sampler, and texture cache are already resident.
  The shortcut is deliberately exact: initialized/acquired-frame state, the
  generic (non-lightmap/non-filter) program, bound programs, a current MVP,
