- v1.92 repairs the exact 60-to-30 Hz presentation schedule for every visual
  configuration. The prior divider consumed its second VBlank before input,
  simulation, command generation, and rendering, so a nominal 33.3 ms frame
  still had only about 16.7 ms of useful work time before its flip deadline.
  The completed prior flip now starts the next frame immediately. At EndFrame,
  completed commands are flushed so RSX can work during the intermediate
  VBlank; only the following flip command waits for that queue boundary. FIFO
  ordering still prevents presentation before rendering completes, XMB callback
