- v1.85 makes the verified PS3 presentation fence authoritative for native
  refresh and exact 60-to-30 Hz pacing. The previous scheduler waited for the
  flip/VBlank interval and then compared the resulting integer-microsecond
  sample against the same interval expressed as a floating-point threshold.
  A 16,666 us sample could consequently reject a completed 16,666.67 us 60 Hz
  slot, or a 33,332 us sample could reject an exact two-VBlank 30 Hz slot,
  delaying that frame after the hardware had already proved it ready. A
  successfully completed fence now directly authorizes the render pass; first
  frame, timeout, callback interruption, VSync-off, timedemo, 50 Hz/non-exact
  30 Hz, and arbitrary non-divisible caps retain the bounded software path.
  This cadence correction is independent of Custom/720p/1080p, filters,
  framebuffer layout, quality, and mono/stereo. The exact-divisor prewait also
  no longer reports success after its counter timeout. v1.84 hierarchical BSP
  clipping and v1.83 deterministic explicit-triangle text remain active. This
  is an update-only physical-test release; no RPCS3 resources were used.
- v1.84 makes world frustum culling hierarchical. The old traversal tested all
  four frustum planes against every PVS-visible BSP node. Each node now carries
  only the planes crossed by its parent; once the parent's negative support
  corner is in front of a plane, that bit is removed for the complete enclosed
  subtree. The positive support corner and strict outside comparison are
  unchanged, preserving exact rejection and surface visibility. A 500,000-case
  randomized equivalence/containment test produced zero outside mismatches and
  zero invalid inherited-plane eliminations. `ps3_rsx_stats 1` now reports
  `world_clip_tests` and `world_clip_skips`; the latter counts node/plane pairs
